Id: cron002i
Severity: INFO
Category: cron
Check: check_crontabs
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

The listed cron entry uses an executable or file which is not owned
by the owner of the cron entry, and is also not owned by a system
account (root or bin, etc).  For root cron entries, these are especially
dangerous.  Note that the actual problem may be with a directory in
the path to the file, not the file itself.

It is INFO rather than a WARN because the owner expected is root and
the file named is a directory or not executable: whoever owns it can
change what it holds, but not a program that runs.

Until 3.4.0 this was reported as cron002, without the letter for its level.
